hi this is presto occur in this video  IVA riddle for you alright I'm somewhere  on earth I walk one mile south one mile  west and one mile north I end up exactly  back where I started where am i this  puzzle has a long history in the tech  industry Microsoft would famously ask it  as one of its technical brain teasers  Elon Musk who co-founded PayPal and  Tesla Motors also admits this is one of  his favorite riddles so can you figure  it out where did I start after I walk  one mile south one mile west and one  mile north and ended up exactly back  where I started  first of all I should tell you there is  a solution in fact there is more than  one spot that's a huge hint I'm gonna  give you so give this puzzle a try  when you're ready continue watching the  video and I'll explain what the solution  is  all right so let's imagine the earth as  a perfect sphere one spot that's the  answer is the North Pole if you're  starting at the North Pole when you go  one mile south then one mile west and  finally one mile north you will go on a  triangular path and end up exactly back  at the North Pole so this is one answer  to the puzzle and this is what most  people think about in fact there are  many more answers to this puzzle so  let's think about our perfectly  spherical earth now let's think about  some places near the South Pole imagine  a circle that is exactly one mile around  in circumference and we're going to have  this really close to the South Pole so  this is not drawn to scale obviously but  think about a circle that's exactly one  mile around very near the south  pull we'll call that circle c1 now  imagine starting exactly one mile north  of this circle so what would happen when  you go one mile south you're going to go  from your starting point to the circle  c1 when you go one mile west you're  going to go exactly one mile around the  circle and come back to your starting  point on that circle and finally when  you go one mile north you're going to  end up back at your starting point so  this is another type of solution to this  puzzle you start one mile north of c1  you'll go down to c1 one mile south then  you'll travel around that circle and  then you'll go back up exactly to your  starting point in fact there's an entire  circle this entire circle that's one  mile north of c1 is all a set of  possible answers so this is an infinite  number of infinite number of points that  you could start it that are one mile  north of c1 so we already know that  north pole is an answer this is an  infinite number of answers that you can  also add but the puzzle gets more  interesting now let's consider a circle  that's exactly 1/2 mile around so it's  going to be very near the South Pole and  it's exactly 1/2 mile around in  circumference we can think about exactly  the same solution if we are one mile  north of this circle see 1/2 we will go  one mile south to the circle now when we  go one mile west we're going to traverse  this circle exactly two times and then  we're going to go one mile north and end  up back at the starting point so think  about how this works you go one mile  south towards C 1/2 then when you go one  mile west you're going to go around the  circle two times and then you're going  to return one mile north exactly to  where you started and once again there  are an infinite number of these points  because  you can be anywhere along the circle  that's one mile north of C 1/2 so you  could start anywhere that's one mile  north of C 1/2 and that's another  infinite set of solutions we can  generalize this let's think about a  circle that's 1 over n miles around and  we want n to be a whole number so we  have 1/3 1/4 etc if you start 1 mile  north of C 1 over N you're going to go  one mile south to that circle then  you're going to go around that circle n  times because the circle has a  circumference of 1 over n and then  you're going to go one mile north and  end up exactly where you started once  again there's an infinite number of  solutions here because you can start  anywhere along the circle that's one  mile north of c1 over N so got it you  can start anywhere that's one mile north  of c1 over N where n is an integer and  that's the complete set of solutions one  answer is you could be at the North Pole  you'll trace out a triangular path  another set of solutions is you can be  one mile north of c1 so this is a circle  that's exactly one mile in circumference  and you can be anywhere on the circle  that's one mile north of it that's an  infinite number of spots you could also  be one mile north of c1 over two so  that's a circle with a circumference of  1 over 2 this is another infinite set of  solutions and you could really do this  for C one mile north of C 1 over n and  of course this 1 over n can be true for  any positive integer n so you can be any  one mile north of C 1 over n C 1 over n  has an infinite number solutions and one  mile north of it there's also an  infinite number of spots that you can  start from so the answer to this puzzle  is there's one plus infinity times  infinity so it's a really cool  brain teaser you can ask it to people  and almost no one gets to answer correct  I hope you liked this video please  subscribe to my channel I make videos on  math and game theory you can catch me on  my blog mind your decisions which you  can follow on Facebook Google+ and  patreon you can also catch me on social  media at pressure Locker on a bunch of  sites I've listed links in the  description and please check out my  books if you like this puzzle I've  written several books about math puzzles  there's a link to all my books in the  video description thanks for watching
 

